# Spend Guard proxy: manual test cases.
# Open in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension and click "Send Request" above each block.
#
# Setup (once):
#   npm run dev:proxy
#   export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...   (and/or OPENAI_API_KEY)
#   npm run cli -w apps/proxy -- setup --login you --project "Manual tests" --provider anthropic --daily 0.05 --rpm 20
#   npm run cli -w apps/proxy -- provider-key --project <project id> --provider openai
# Paste the printed apg_live_ key below. Real calls cost real (tiny) amounts: Haiku is ~$0.0003 here.

@base = http://localhost:8090
@key = apg_live_PASTE_YOUR_KEY_HERE

### 1. Readiness
GET {{base}}/readyz

### 2. No key: refused in Anthropic's error format
POST {{base}}/anthropic/v1/messages
content-type: application/json

{}

### 3. A raw provider key: refused, with an explanation
POST {{base}}/openai/v1/chat/completions
authorization: Bearer sk-proj-not-a-spend-guard-key
content-type: application/json

{"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "hi"}]}

### 4. Anthropic, plain. Look for the x-apg-cost-usd response header.
POST {{base}}/anthropic/v1/messages
x-api-key: {{key}}
anthropic-version: 2023-06-01
content-type: application/json

{"model": "claude-haiku-4-5", "max_tokens": 50, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Say hello in five words."}]}

### 5. Anthropic, streaming: events arrive as they are generated
POST {{base}}/anthropic/v1/messages
x-api-key: {{key}}
content-type: application/json

{"model": "claude-haiku-4-5", "max_tokens": 50, "stream": true, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Count to five."}]}

### 6. Per-request limit: a huge max_tokens is refused before anything is sent
# (needs a key created with --max-request, e.g. 0.25)
POST {{base}}/anthropic/v1/messages
x-api-key: {{key}}
content-type: application/json

{"model": "claude-haiku-4-5", "max_tokens": 64000, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "hi"}]}

### 7. Unknown model: blocked, because it can't be priced
POST {{base}}/anthropic/v1/messages
x-api-key: {{key}}
content-type: application/json

{"model": "claude-made-up-9", "max_tokens": 10, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "hi"}]}

### 8. OpenAI chat (needs the OpenAI provider key stored)
POST {{base}}/openai/v1/chat/completions
authorization: Bearer {{key}}
content-type: application/json

{"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "max_tokens": 30, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Say hi."}]}

### 9. OpenAI chat streaming: no extra usage chunk appears, yet the cost is still recorded
POST {{base}}/openai/v1/chat/completions
authorization: Bearer {{key}}
content-type: application/json

{"model": "gpt-4o-mini", "max_tokens": 30, "stream": true, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Say hi."}]}

### 10. Unsupported endpoint
POST {{base}}/openai/v1/embeddings
authorization: Bearer {{key}}
content-type: application/json

{"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "input": "hi"}

### 11. Free endpoint: listed models, not billed
GET {{base}}/anthropic/v1/models
x-api-key: {{key}}

# Next: run `npm run cli -w apps/proxy -- usage --project <id>` to see every request above,
# including the blocked ones, with their cost. Then try `freeze --key <id>` and resend #4.
